<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch Nov cash retail sales rise 4.4 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Dutch Nov cash retail sales rise 4.4 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>VOORBURG, Netherlands 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch retail sales rose 4.4 percent in cash terms in November compared with November 1995, the Central Bureau of Statistics (CBS) said.</p>
<p>In volume terms November retail sales were 4.1 percent higher than in November 1995, the CBS added.  </p>
<p>DUTCH RETAIL SALES		     Nov 96    Oct 96	 Nov 95</p>
<p> Pct change cash yr/yr		   4.4	10.0	    3.5</p>
<p>     index (base 1994)		   109	 110	    104</p>
<p> Pct change prices yr/yr		 0.2	 0.5	   -0.7</p>
<p> Pct change volume yr/yr		 4.1	 9.5	    4.2</p>
<p>     index (base 1994)		   109	 109	    104</p>
<p> DUTCH RETAIL SALES IN DETAIL	Nov 96   Oct 96   Jan/Nov 96</p>
<p>						     (pct changes yr/yr)</p>
<p> Food cash				  +6.6     +9.7	   +3.5</p>
<p> Food prices				+0.6     +0.6	   -0.1</p>
<p> Food volume				+6.0     +9.1	   +3.6</p>
<p> Durable goods &amp; non-food cash	+2.9    +10.2	   +4.1</p>
<p> Durable goods &amp; non-food prices    -0.1     +0.2	   -0.1</p>
<p> Durable goods &amp; non-food volume    +3.0     +9.9	   +4.2</p>
<p>NOTE - November 1996 comprised one Wednesday and one Thursday fewer and had one more Friday and Saturday than in the same month a year earlier.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
</text>
